# F'(a) at a point.  The at-a-point path (calc2_syntax.inc) calls
# tidy(diff_node(...)) directly, bypassing the old has_fma/simp_diff workaround.
# Before the IS_OP3 fix this failed with "internal: fma lost its third operand
# in a generic rebuild"; now it returns a number even though the derivative
# still contains an fma.
F(x) = sin(fma(x,x,x))
F'(1)
G(x) = fma(x,x,x)^2
G'(2)
H(x) = fma(x,x,x)
H'(1)
K(x) = cos(fma(x,x,x))
K''(1)
K'''(1)
